<p>A <code>Path</code> is a drawing surface you add to a page, and every shape it can draw is a method on it.</p>
<h2 id="adding-a-path-to-a-page">Adding a Path to a Page<a class="anchor" href="#adding-a-path-to-a-page" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p>Construct a path, draw on it, and hand it to a page with <code>addPath()</code>:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Path</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Color\Color\Rgb</span>;

<span class="text-var">$path</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Path</span>(<span class="text-type">Path</span>::<span class="text-num">FILL</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setFillColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">102</span>, <span class="text-num">204</span>));
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawRectangle</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">200</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">h</span>: <span class="text-num">150</span>);

<span class="text-var">$page</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Page</span>(<span class="text-type">Page</span>::<span class="text-num">LETTER</span>);
<span class="text-var">$page</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addPath</span>(<span class="text-var">$path</span>);

<span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">writeToFile</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>(<span class="text-var">$page</span>), <span class="text-type">filename</span>: <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/shapes.pdf&#039;</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>The constructor argument sets the paint style and defaults to <code>Path::STROKE</code> — see <a href="#path-styles">Path
Styles</a> for the full set. Coordinates are PDF points measured from the bottom left
corner of the page (see <a href="/build/pages#the-coordinate-system">Pages &amp; Coordinates</a>), and every
coordinate on every method takes an <code>int</code> or a <code>float</code>.</p>
<p><code>addPath()</code> returns the page and every <code>draw*</code> method returns the path, so calls chain either way. A
page holds as many paths as it needs, each with its own style, colors and stroke width:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
