<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Path</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Color\Color\Rgb</span>;

<span class="text-var">$path</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Path</span>();
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setStrokeColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>));
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setStroke</span>(<span class="text-num">1</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawLine</span>(<span class="text-type">x1</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-type">y1</span>: <span class="text-num">400</span>, <span class="text-type">x2</span>: <span class="text-num">400</span>, <span class="text-type">y2</span>: <span class="text-num">400</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>A line always strokes, regardless of the path's style, taking its color from <code>setStrokeColor()</code> and
width/dash from <code>setStroke()</code>.</p>
<h3 id="rectangles-and-squares">Rectangles and Squares<a class="anchor" href="#rectangles-and-squares" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>

<p><code>drawRectangle($x, $y, $w, $h = null)</code> places its lower left corner at <code>$x, $y</code> and extends right and
up. <code>drawSquare($x, $y, $w)</code> is the same call with one dimension:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Path</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Color\Color\Rgb</span>;

<span class="text-var">$path</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Path</span>(<span class="text-type">Path</span>::<span class="text-num">FILL</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setFillColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">102</span>, <span class="text-num">204</span>));
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawRectangle</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">550</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">h</span>: <span class="text-num">150</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawSquare</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">350</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">150</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<h3 id="rounded-rectangles-and-squares">Rounded Rectangles and Squares<a class="anchor" href="#rounded-rectangles-and-squares" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>

<p><code>drawRoundedRectangle($x, $y, $w, $h = null, $rx = 10, $ry = null)</code> and
<code>drawRoundedSquare($x, $y, $w, $rx = 10, $ry = null)</code> take the same origin and dimensions plus two
corner radii. <code>$rx</code> is the horizontal radius and <code>$ry</code> the vertical one; leave <code>$ry</code> off and it
matches <code>$rx</code>:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Path</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Color\Color\Rgb</span>;

<span class="text-var">$path</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Path</span>(<span class="text-type">Path</span>::<span class="text-num">FILL</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setFillColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">102</span>, <span class="text-num">204</span>));
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawRoundedRectangle</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">200</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">h</span>: <span class="text-num">150</span>, <span class="text-type">rx</span>: <span class="text-num">40</span>, <span class="text-type">ry</span>: <span class="text-num">20</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>The radii carve into the corners; the bounding box itself is unchanged.</p>
<h3 id="polygons">Polygons<a class="anchor" href="#polygons" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>

<p><code>drawPolygon()</code> takes an array of points, each with an <code>x</code> and <code>y</code> key, closes the outline back to the
first point, and paints itself in the path's style — as of 6.0.7; earlier versions emitted no paint
operator at all:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Path</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Color\Color\Rgb</span>;

<span class="text-var">$path</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Path</span>(<span class="text-type">Path</span>::<span class="text-num">FILL_STROKE</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setFillColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">230</span>, <span class="text-num">230</span>, <span class="text-num">230</span>));
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setStrokeColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>));
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setStroke</span>(<span class="text-num">2</span>);

<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawPolygon</span>(<span class="text-type">points</span>: [
    [<span class="text-str">&#039;x&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;y&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">400</span>],
    [<span class="text-str">&#039;x&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">250</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;y&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">520</span>],
    [<span class="text-str">&#039;x&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">400</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;y&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">400</span>],
]);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Every point needs both keys — one missing either raises <code>Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Exception</code>.</p>
<h3 id="ellipses-and-circles">Ellipses and Circles<a class="anchor" href="#ellipses-and-circles" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>

<p><code>drawEllipse($x, $y, $w, $h = null)</code> and <code>drawCircle($x, $y, $w)</code> are centered on <code>$x, $y</code>, and <code>$w</code>
and <code>$h</code> are the horizontal and vertical <strong>radii</strong> rather than the full width and height:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Path</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Color\Color\Rgb</span>;

<span class="text-var">$path</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Path</span>(<span class="text-type">Path</span>::<span class="text-num">FILL</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setFillColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">102</span>, <span class="text-num">204</span>));
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawEllipse</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">600</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">150</span>, <span class="text-type">h</span>: <span class="text-num">75</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawCircle</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">400</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="arcs-chords-and-pies">Arcs, Chords and Pies<a class="anchor" href="#arcs-chords-and-pies" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>drawArc()</code>, <code>drawChord()</code> and <code>drawPie()</code> share one signature — <code>($x, $y, $start, $end, $w, $h = null)</code> — with <code>$x, $y</code> the center and <code>$w</code>/<code>$h</code> the radii, as with an ellipse. Angles are degrees
counterclockwise from 3 o'clock, so <code>0, 90</code> sweeps the upper right quadrant:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Path</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Color\Color\Rgb</span>;

<span class="text-var">$path</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Path</span>(<span class="text-type">Path</span>::<span class="text-num">FILL</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setFillColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">102</span>, <span class="text-num">204</span>));
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawPie</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">200</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">600</span>, <span class="text-type">start</span>: <span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-type">end</span>: <span class="text-num">90</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">120</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawChord</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">450</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">600</span>, <span class="text-type">start</span>: <span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-type">end</span>: <span class="text-num">90</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">120</span>);

<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setStyle</span>(<span class="text-type">Path</span>::<span class="text-num">STROKE</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setStrokeColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>));
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setStroke</span>(<span class="text-num">3</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawArc</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">start</span>: <span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-type">end</span>: <span class="text-num">270</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">120</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>The three differ only in how the sweep closes:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>arc</strong> — the curve alone, usually stroked</li>
<li><strong>chord</strong> — closed with a straight line between the end points, filling the segment above it</li>
<li><strong>pie</strong> — closed through the center, filling the whole wedge</li>
</ul>
<p>Start must be 0 or more, end 360 or less, and start less than end — any other pair raises
<code>OutOfRangeException</code> naming the rule broken. Sweeps over 90 degrees split into several curve segments
internally, so <code>0, 270</code> draws as one continuous arc.</p>
<h2 id="b-zier-curves">Bézier Curves<a class="anchor" href="#b-zier-curves" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<h3 id="cubic">Cubic<a class="anchor" href="#cubic" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>

<p><code>drawOpenCubicBezierCurve($x1, $y1, $x2, $y2, $bezierX1, $bezierY1, $bezierX2, $bezierY2)</code> takes the
two end points first and the two control points after them:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Path</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Color\Color\Rgb</span>;

<span class="text-var">$path</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Path</span>();
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setStrokeColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>));
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setStroke</span>(<span class="text-num">3</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawOpenCubicBezierCurve</span>(
    <span class="text-type">x1</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-type">y1</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">x2</span>: <span class="text-num">400</span>, <span class="text-type">y2</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>,
    <span class="text-type">bezierX1</span>: <span class="text-num">175</span>, <span class="text-type">bezierY1</span>: <span class="text-num">550</span>, <span class="text-type">bezierX2</span>: <span class="text-num">325</span>, <span class="text-type">bezierY2</span>: <span class="text-num">550</span>
);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p><code>drawClosedCubicBezierCurve()</code> takes the identical eight arguments and adds the straight segment back
to the start point, so a stroke style outlines that segment too.</p>
<h3 id="quadratic">Quadratic<a class="anchor" href="#quadratic" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>

<p><code>drawOpenQuadraticBezierCurve($x1, $y1, $x2, $y2, $bezierX, $bezierY, $first = true)</code> steers with a
single control point, and <code>$first</code> decides which end that point is anchored to:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Path</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Color\Color\Rgb</span>;

<span class="text-var">$path</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Path</span>();
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setStrokeColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>));
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setStroke</span>(<span class="text-num">2</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawOpenQuadraticBezierCurve</span>(
    <span class="text-type">x1</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-type">y1</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">x2</span>: <span class="text-num">500</span>, <span class="text-type">y2</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">bezierX</span>: <span class="text-num">150</span>, <span class="text-type">bezierY</span>: <span class="text-num">600</span>
);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawOpenQuadraticBezierCurve</span>(
    <span class="text-type">x1</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-type">y1</span>: <span class="text-num">200</span>, <span class="text-type">x2</span>: <span class="text-num">500</span>, <span class="text-type">y2</span>: <span class="text-num">200</span>, <span class="text-type">bezierX</span>: <span class="text-num">150</span>, <span class="text-type">bezierY</span>: <span class="text-num">500</span>, <span class="text-type">first</span>: <span class="text-num">false</span>
);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p><code>true</code>, the default, anchors the control point to the curve's start; <code>false</code> anchors it to the end.
<code>drawClosedQuadraticBezierCurve()</code> takes the same seven arguments and closes back to the start,
outlined the same way the closed cubic form is.</p>
<h2 id="layers">Layers<a class="anchor" href="#layers" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>openLayer()</code> and <code>closeLayer()</code> save and restore the graphics state around a run of drawing — colors,
stroke settings and clipping applied inside are discarded when it closes, and whatever was in force
before returns:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Path</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Color\Color\Rgb</span>;

<span class="text-var">$path</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Path</span>(<span class="text-type">Path</span>::<span class="text-num">FILL</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setFillColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>));

<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">openLayer</span>()
     -&gt;<span class="text-fn">setFillColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">200</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>))
     -&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawSquare</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">500</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">120</span>)
     -&gt;<span class="text-fn">closeLayer</span>();

<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawSquare</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">500</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">120</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>The red set inside the layer lasts until <code>closeLayer()</code>; the black set before the layer is what the
second square picks up once it closes.</p>
<p>Layers nest, and each <code>closeLayer()</code> restores the state its matching <code>openLayer()</code> saved:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Path</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Color\Color\Rgb</span>;

<span class="text-var">$path</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Path</span>(<span class="text-type">Path</span>::<span class="text-num">FILL</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setFillColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>));

<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">openLayer</span>()
     -&gt;<span class="text-fn">setFillColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">200</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>))
     -&gt;<span class="text-fn">openLayer</span>()
     -&gt;<span class="text-fn">setFillColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">150</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>))
     -&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawSquare</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">400</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">80</span>)
     -&gt;<span class="text-fn">closeLayer</span>()
     -&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawSquare</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">220</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">400</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">80</span>)
     -&gt;<span class="text-fn">closeLayer</span>();

<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawSquare</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">340</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">400</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">80</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Innermost first, those three squares come out green, red and black.</p>
<p>A path keeps its drawing as a list of content stream fragments, and <code>getStreams()</code> hands that list
back. Opening a layer appends the PDF graphics state save operator and closing one appends the
restore:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Path</span>;

<span class="text-var">$path</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Path</span>();
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">openLayer</span>()-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawLine</span>(<span class="text-type">x1</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-type">y1</span>: <span class="text-num">400</span>, <span class="text-type">x2</span>: <span class="text-num">400</span>, <span class="text-type">y2</span>: <span class="text-num">400</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">closeLayer</span>();

<span class="text-kw">foreach</span> (<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getStreams</span>() <span class="text-kw">as</span> <span class="text-var">$stream</span>) {
    <span class="text-kw">echo</span> <span class="text-fn">trim</span>(<span class="text-var">$stream</span>[<span class="text-str">&#039;stream&#039;</span>]) . <span class="text-str">&quot;\n&quot;</span>;
}
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>That prints <code>q</code>, the line's two point placeholders, its <code>S</code> operator, then <code>Q</code>. The placeholders hold
coordinates unresolved until the document compiles, against whatever origin is in force then.</p>
<h2 id="path-styles">Path Styles<a class="anchor" href="#path-styles" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p>The style is what the path does with each finished shape. <code>setStyle()</code> sets it, and every shape drawn
after the call uses the new value, so one path can fill one shape and outline the next:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Path</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Color\Color\Rgb</span>;

<span class="text-var">$path</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Path</span>(<span class="text-type">Path</span>::<span class="text-num">FILL</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setFillColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">102</span>, <span class="text-num">204</span>));
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setStrokeColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">0</span>));
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setStroke</span>(<span class="text-num">3</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawRectangle</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">200</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-type">h</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>);

<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setStyle</span>(<span class="text-type">Path</span>::<span class="text-num">STROKE</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawRectangle</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">200</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-type">h</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>The first rectangle is solid blue; the second, a black outline. Pass the constants themselves rather
than their string values — <code>setStyle()</code> keeps the style the path already has for any other value, and
<code>getStyle()</code> reports the one currently in force.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Constant</th>
<th>Paints</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>Path::STROKE</code></td>
<td>the outline</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Path::STROKE_CLOSE</code></td>
<td>the outline, with the shape closed back to its start point first</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Path::FILL</code></td>
<td>the interior</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Path::FILL_EVEN_ODD</code></td>
<td>the interior, under the even-odd rule</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Path::FILL_STROKE</code></td>
<td>the interior, then the outline over it</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Path::FILL_STROKE_EVEN_ODD</code></td>
<td>both, filling under the even-odd rule</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Path::FILL_STROKE_CLOSE</code></td>
<td>both, with the shape closed first</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Path::FILL_STROKE_CLOSE_EVEN_ODD</code></td>
<td>both, closed first and filled under the even-odd rule</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Path::CLIPPING</code></td>
<td>nothing, and adds the shape to the clipping region, leaving the path open for the next shape to join</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Path::CLIPPING_FILL</code></td>
<td>the interior, and clips to the shape</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Path::CLIPPING_NO_STYLE</code></td>
<td>nothing, and clips under the nonzero winding rule, ending the path there</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Path::CLIPPING_EVEN_ODD</code></td>
<td>nothing, and clips under the even-odd rule, leaving the path open for the next shape to join</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Path::CLIPPING_EVEN_ODD_FILL</code></td>
<td>the interior, and clips under the even-odd rule</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Path::CLIPPING_EVEN_ODD_NO_STYLE</code></td>
<td>nothing, and clips under the even-odd rule, ending the path there</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Path::NO_STYLE</code></td>
<td>nothing — the shape contributes its geometry and no ink</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3 id="even-odd-filling">Even-Odd Filling<a class="anchor" href="#even-odd-filling" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>

<p>The plain fill styles use the nonzero winding rule; the <code>EVEN_ODD</code> variants use the even-odd rule.
They agree on a single shape and diverge only when one outline sits inside another on the same path —
that's how a hole gets cut. Since every shape paints itself as soon as it's drawn, cutting a hole
needs <code>openPath()</code> and <code>paintPath()</code> to hold several outlines on one path and paint them together:
shapes drawn between the two calls contribute outlines without painting, and <code>paintPath()</code> emits the
style once for all of them.</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Path</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Color\Color\Rgb</span>;

<span class="text-var">$path</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Path</span>(<span class="text-type">Path</span>::<span class="text-num">FILL_EVEN_ODD</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setFillColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">102</span>, <span class="text-num">204</span>));

<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">openPath</span>();
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawPolygon</span>(<span class="text-type">points</span>: [
    [<span class="text-str">&#039;x&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">150</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;y&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">250</span>], [<span class="text-str">&#039;x&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">450</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;y&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">250</span>],
    [<span class="text-str">&#039;x&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">450</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;y&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">550</span>], [<span class="text-str">&#039;x&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">150</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;y&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">550</span>],
]);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawPolygon</span>(<span class="text-type">points</span>: [
    [<span class="text-str">&#039;x&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">250</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;y&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">350</span>], [<span class="text-str">&#039;x&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">350</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;y&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">350</span>],
    [<span class="text-str">&#039;x&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">350</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;y&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">450</span>], [<span class="text-str">&#039;x&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">250</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;y&#039;</span> =&gt; <span class="text-num">450</span>],
]);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">paintPath</span>();
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>That fills a 300-point square with a blank 100-point hole — an 80,000-point ring. Swap in
<code>Path::FILL</code> and the same two outlines fill solid, all 90,000 points. Skip <code>openPath()</code> and the two
<code>drawPolygon()</code> calls each paint themselves as drawn — one solid square stacked on another, since
even-odd only cuts a hole when it reads both outlines from a single path.</p>
<h3 id="clipping">Clipping<a class="anchor" href="#clipping" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>

<p>A clipping style turns a shape into a mask for everything drawn after it on the same path. Set
<code>Path::CLIPPING_NO_STYLE</code> — usable as of 6.0.7, silently ignored as an unrecognized style before it —
or <code>Path::CLIPPING_EVEN_ODD_NO_STYLE</code>, draw the mask, switch to a paint style, and draw the content
inside a layer so the mask lifts at <code>closeLayer()</code>:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Path</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Color\Color\Rgb</span>;

<span class="text-var">$path</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Path</span>(<span class="text-type">Path</span>::<span class="text-num">CLIPPING_EVEN_ODD_NO_STYLE</span>);
<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">openLayer</span>()-&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawCircle</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">400</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>);

<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setStyle</span>(<span class="text-type">Path</span>::<span class="text-num">FILL</span>)
     -&gt;<span class="text-fn">setFillColor</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Rgb</span>(<span class="text-num">0</span>, <span class="text-num">102</span>, <span class="text-num">204</span>))
     -&gt;<span class="text-fn">drawRectangle</span>(<span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">200</span>, <span class="text-type">w</span>: <span class="text-num">400</span>, <span class="text-type">h</span>: <span class="text-num">400</span>);

<span class="text-var">$path</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">closeLayer</span>();
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>The 400-point square comes out as a 200-point blue disc — only the part inside the circle reaches the
page. <code>Path::CLIPPING_NO_STYLE</code> reads the mask under the nonzero winding rule and
<code>Path::CLIPPING_EVEN_ODD_NO_STYLE</code> under the even-odd rule; a single circle gives them nothing to
disagree about, so both produce the same disc here. The choice matters only once the mask combines
more than one outline, as in <a href="#even-odd-filling">Even-Odd Filling</a>. <code>Path::CLIPPING_FILL</code> and
<code>Path::CLIPPING_EVEN_ODD_FILL</code> clip the same way and also paint the mask shape in the fill color, so
the circle stays visible under whatever the clip lets through.</p>
